Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:08:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 087/154] feat(sidebar): a navigation row beside the traffic
 lights
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Back, forward and reload move to the right edge of the row, animate on press,
grey out when the tab cannot go that way, fold into an overflow menu on a
narrow sidebar, and move into the floating address bar while it is up.

Option and Cmd+Shift widen all three: to the first or last page of the tab and
a hard reload, or the previous or next page in a new tab and a hard reload
that clears the site's cookies and storage first. The modifier state is pushed
from the process-wide flagsChanged monitor, since the page only sees key
events while it holds the keyboard.

The glyphs come from the lab: 17px text glyphs in a 22px box, a 16px reload
arc with a bolt for the hard reload and a dashed arc with crumbs for the
clearing one, on filled amber and red plates rather than the lab's
translucent ones, which measured under 2:1 on a light tint.

NonClientHitTest's caption carve moves to atrium_nav_carve_decision so the
geometry tracks the sidebar width and has a unit test of its own.

The bar.append line that adds the pin beside the nav group is tangled with
the address bar pin, and lands with that change.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
